# Line endings: LF in every checkout, Windows included. Git for Windows converts text files to CRLF by default
# (core.autocrlf=true), and SUDS reads some of them byte for byte: server/schema.sql (its migrations match
# "\n);" and split on "\n"), the generated server/schema-text.js and public/local/kernel.js that CI compares with
# a rebuild, the shell scripts a Linux server runs, signed evidence and fixtures. A clone on Windows and a
# GitHub "Download ZIP" (git archive applies these rules too) then have the same bytes as a clone on Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never converted: binary files, and transcripts kept exactly as they were captured.
*.png binary
*.gz binary
*.br binary
*.wasm binary
*.zip binary
*.db binary
docs/evidence/** -text
